## Methods

- Protocol `{{ p.run.protocol_id }}`, hash `{{ p.run.protocol_hash[:12] }}`; code `{{ p.run.code_sha }}`.
- Adjudicator {{ p.run.adjudicator.model }} (prompt {{ p.run.adjudicator.prompt_version }}); reader version {{ p.run.reader.read_version }}; report writer {{ p.run.reporter.model or "none (narrative withheld)" }}{% if p.run.reporter.prompt_version %} (prompt {{ p.run.reporter.prompt_version }}){% endif %}.
- Estimator: prediction-powered inference (Angelopoulos et al. 2023, mean estimator) on the estimation pool ({{ p.run.review.estimation_pool_fraction }} of reviews), {{ p.run.review.confidence }} confidence; Wilson intervals for the naive and classical rates. The PPI variance omits the (≥ 0) covariance term, so corrected intervals are conservative.
- Cells with n < {{ p.run.suppress_below }} are suppressed.
- Who reviews the data entered: the clinician, through the review workbench (Confirm, Override, Flag per case); a flagged review is excluded from every estimate. Reviewers on this run: {{ p.quality.reviews.reviewers|join(", ") or "none" }}. Cases with a review on file: {{ p.quality.reviews.n_latest }} (validated {{ p.quality.reviews.n_validated }}, disputed {{ p.quality.reviews.n_disputed }}, flagged {{ p.quality.reviews.n_flagged }}).
- The "by whom" column names the audit lead because the protocol has no field for it.
- Replicable: `auditpace estimate && auditpace report` on the same tables reproduces every figure; estimates computed {{ p.run.estimates_computed_ts }}.

